# Draft OpenDir release

When the user says **draft a release** (or similar), do the full release workflow and **always publish the draft with GitHub CLI (`gh`)** — do not stop at local packaging or tell the user to create the release manually unless `gh` authentication fails after retry.

## Version bump

Read `opendir-extension/package.json`, then bump using the single-digit rule in `opendir-extension/scripts/version.mjs`:

- Increment patch: `0.0.1` → `0.0.2`
- Patch max 9 → next minor: `0.0.9` → `0.1.0`
- Minor max 9 → next major: `0.9.9` → `1.0.0`

Run:

```bash
cd opendir-extension
node scripts/bump-version.mjs
```

Update `CHANGELOG.md` with the new version section before committing.

## Build and package

```bash
cd opendir-extension
npm test
npm run build
node scripts/package-release.mjs
```

This produces `release/OpenDir-<version>.zip`.

## Draft with gh (required)

Commit, push the working branch, then create a **draft** release:

```bash
gh release create v<version> \
  --draft \
  --title "OpenDir <version>" \
  --target <branch-name> \
  --notes-file opendir-extension/RELEASE.md \
  release/OpenDir-<version>.zip
```

Use `--draft` unless the user explicitly asks to publish.

If a prior draft for the same tag exists, delete or update it with `gh release delete` / `gh release edit` as appropriate.

## On gh auth failure

If `gh` returns 401, still commit and push all release changes, then tell the user `gh auth login` is required and provide the exact `gh release create` command to run locally.
